      e_mode` allowed values as `generic_government / enterprise_crisis / public_figure`, but the actual code in `src
      /analysis/risk_analyzer.py` (lines 96-102) and `src/phase4/report_agent.py` (line 152-156) only ever produces `
      law_enforcement_facing / regulator_facing / public_management_facing / generic_government` via the `AudienceMod
      e` enum from `src.schemas.phase4`. The other three enum values appear nowhere in the listed target files. This
      is a documentation/spec drift, not a runtime bug — the spec YAML drives a downstream rendering, so the generato
      r that reads this spec will mislabel the field for any value it doesn't know about. Recommended action: update
      `spec/dataset_fields.yaml` to match the actual `AudienceMode` enum.
